  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b3b563d715eb6c64c9b6c779e47f3352, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day5Martha
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Category: 2
  Prefab: {fileID: 6625514644646704096, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  Interactable: {fileID: 5048261325816738630, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  TextFields:
  - 
  - "Dear Astrid,\r\n\r\nI got your letter yesterday\u2014finally. Mail\u2019s slow
    as ever. I read it twice, and I just have to say: I\u2019m worried about you.\r\n\r\nI
    heard from your dad that he likely won\u2019t be making it back this season.
    I know you\u2019ll take it like you always do\u2014quiet and strong\u2014but
    I also know you were hoping. I was too.\r\n\r\nPlease don\u2019t try to stay
    up there all winter by yourself. I know you think you can handle it. And maybe
    you can. But should you? That\u2019s a different question. Even the toughest
    people start to unravel a little when the wind never stops and the only sound
    is the ice shifting at night.\r\n\r\nAnd Elijah\u2014well, you said in your letter
    he\u2019s planning to come back. But he\u2019s a lot like your dad, isn\u2019t
    he? Brilliant, yes, but he gets that faraway look and suddenly there\u2019s nothing
    in the world but the next set of data. I know he loves you, but loving someone
    doesn\u2019t mean they show up on time.\r\n\r\nI know, I know\u2014Astrology...
    I mean, Astronomy, is important. (I always mix that up\u2014I can see your eyes
    rolling.) You think the satellite, the sky, the signals\u2014all of it\u2014will
    help put things back together. Maybe it will. But honey, people are hurting now.
    Not in the stars. Here, on the ground. You were so good at caring for them. I
    miss watching you work at the clinic. I love working with you and we laughed
    together so much even on the hard days. \r\n\r\nI know you were tired. I get
    it. But there are other ways to help that don\u2019t require freezing half to
    death in a tin observatory tower.\r\n\r\nIf Elijah does come back\u2014he\u2019s
    welcome here. We\u2019ve got space. I don\u2019t expect he\u2019ll want to leave
    CERES 12, but he\u2019d eat better if he did. And frankly, so would you. You\u2019re
    not Madame Curie and Pierre. You two don\u2019t have to die glowing in the dark
    to prove a point.\r\n\r\nI love you. I\u2019m proud of you. But I also want you
    to come home -  at least come down for a little while. Let me feed you. We've
    alway been here for each other. \n\nWith love (and worry),\r\nMartha"
  - "P.S. If you write back, tell me something besides \u201CI'm fine.\u201D You
    always say you\u2019re fine."
  StreamingVisuals: []
  DefaultPinnedPos: {x: -1, y: 1.45, z: 0}
